# SCRIPT: txn_Begin
# FOLDER: 00_APP
# ROLE: open a pseudo-transaction — establish ONE parent record as the write anchor
# CALLED BY: every routine that writes more than one record
# CALLS: nothing
# INPUTS: $p (JSON) — { "parentTable":<req>, "parentID":<req>, "label":<opt> }
# GLOBALS IN: none
# RETURNS: { ok, txnID, parentTable, parentID } | { ok:false, error }
# GLOBALS OUT: $$TXN_ACTIVE, $$TXN_ID, $$TXN_PARENT_TABLE, $$TXN_PARENT_ID, $$TXN_LABEL
# SIDE EFFECTS: navigates to the parent's layout and isolates the parent record. Writes NO data.
#
# 🚨 THERE IS NO ENGINE TRANSACTION UNDERNEATH THIS. READ THAT AGAIN.
#   FileMaker 19 has no `Open Transaction` step — it arrived in FileMaker 2023 (v20).
#   Verified against the Claris FMP 20.1.2 release notes and the MBS step-by-version table.
#   The name `txn_Begin` is a CONVENTION borrowed from databases that really have one.
#   If you read this name and assume ACID, you will design something that loses money.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY PROVIDES ATOMICITY:
#   FileMaker holds an uncommitted record and all its RELATED records in one open state
#   until something commits. So if every write in the routine reaches its table THROUGH
#   ONE RELATIONSHIP FROM ONE PARENT RECORD, a single `Revert Record` on that parent
#   discards the entire set. That is the whole mechanism. It is 20 years old and it works.
#
# THEREFORE THE TWO RULES THAT MATTER MORE THAN THIS SCRIPT:
#   1. ONE parent. If a routine legitimately has two parents, it CANNOT be atomic on 19 —
#      split it, or restructure so the real parent is higher. This is why ReceivedFunds
#      had to exist before this wrapper: one check across two loans has two Loans parents,
#      but only ONE receipt.
#   2. NO `Commit Records` between Begin and Commit. Not one. A stray commit ends the
#      transaction and makes everything before it permanent — while the wrapper still
#      reports success. That is the silent-partial-rollback failure, and it is worse than
#      having no rollback at all, because you believe you were protected.
#
# HOW TO USE IT (the shape every write routine takes):
#   Perform Script [ txn_Begin ; { parentTable:"ReceivedFunds", parentID:$rcptID } ]
#   ...all writes, through relationships from that parent...
#   If [ $error ]  Perform Script [ txn_Rollback ]  Exit Script  End If
#   Perform Script [ txn_Commit ]
#
# 🥇 STATE: GOLDEN — designed, not yet built. Build it AFTER tables/ReceivedFunds.md exists.
#
# CHANGELOG:
#   - 2026-07-29 designed. Method ruled by Michael via DL Q3 (rollback + error catching
#     throughout) with Dexter's call that the mechanism and the wrapper are not
#     alternatives: build the classic pattern, then wrap it ONCE so no routine improvises.

# --- SETUP ---
Set Error Capture [ On ]
Set Variable [ $p ; Value: Get ( ScriptParameter ) ]
Set Variable [ $parentTable ; Value: JSONGetElement ( $p ; "parentTable" ) ]
Set Variable [ $parentID ; Value: JSONGetElement ( $p ; "parentID" ) ]
Set Variable [ $label ; Value: JSONGetElement ( $p ; "label" ) ]

If [ IsEmpty ( $parentTable ) or IsEmpty ( $parentID ) ]
	Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; False ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "error" ; "txn_Begin requires parentTable and parentID" ; JSONString ] ) ]
End If

# --- REFUSE TO NEST. A nested pseudo-transaction is a lie: the inner Commit would end the
#     outer one, and the outer Rollback could no longer reach the inner writes. ---
If [ $$TXN_ACTIVE = 1 ]
	Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; False ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "error" ; "transaction already open: " & $$TXN_LABEL ; JSONString ] ) ]
End If

# --- ISOLATE THE PARENT ---
Go to Layout [ $parentTable ]
Enter Find Mode [ Pause: Off ]
Set Field By Name [ $parentTable & "::PrimaryKey" ; $parentID ]
Perform Find [ ]

If [ Get ( FoundCount ) <> 1 ]
	Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; False ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "error" ; "parent not found or not unique" ; JSONString ] ; [ "parentID" ; $parentID ; JSONString ] ) ]
End If

# --- OPEN THE RECORD so FileMaker starts holding uncommitted state on it ---
Open Record/Request

If [ Get ( LastError ) ]
	Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; False ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "error" ; "cannot open parent record (locked?) err " & Get ( LastError ) ; JSONString ] ) ]
End If

# --- ARM THE STATE ---
Set Variable [ $$TXN_ID ; Value: Get ( UUID ) ]
Set Variable [ $$TXN_ACTIVE ; Value: 1 ]
Set Variable [ $$TXN_PARENT_TABLE ; Value: $parentTable ]
Set Variable [ $$TXN_PARENT_ID ; Value: $parentID ]
Set Variable [ $$TXN_LABEL ; Value: Case ( IsEmpty ( $label ) ; "unlabeled" ; $label ) ]

Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; True ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "txnID" ; $$TXN_ID ; JSONString ] ; [ "parentTable" ; $parentTable ; JSONString ] ; [ "parentID" ; $parentID ; JSONString ] ) ]
